0.063 0.094 0.149 rg
40. 301.6500000000000909 Td
(Spread inquiries across bureaus. Experian-leaning: Chase, Amex, Wells Fargo, Bank of America, FNBO, PNC, M&T, TD, USAA.) Tj
T* (TransUnion-leaning: U.S. Bank, Barclays, Synchrony, Navy Federal, Elan, Apple Card. Equifax-leaning: Truist, Citizens, PenFed, DCU,) Tj
T* (Huntington, KeyBank, Target \(TD\). All three: Capital One. Applying to one lender from each group keeps any single report from) Tj
T* (stacking up.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.063 0.094 0.149 rg
40. 250.8500000000001364 Td
(Order by strictest rule first. Chase goes first because of 5/24. Then Amex \(2 cards per 90 days\), then U.S. Bank \(dislikes 5+ new) Tj
T* (accounts in 12 months\), then Wells Fargo, then Bank of America, then regionals. Capital One goes last because it hits all three) Tj
T* (bureaus and most of its business cards report to personal credit.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.063 0.094 0.149 rg
40. 211.7500000000001137 Td
(Soft pulls before hard pulls. Use prequalification tools \(Capital One, Discover, Amex Apply With Confidence, Upstart, Upgrade,) Tj
T* (Fundbox, Capital on Tap\) to see offers before taking a hard inquiry.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.063 0.094 0.149 rg
40. 184.3500000000001364 Td
(Business credit runs in parallel at every tier. Form the entity, get an EIN and D-U-N-S number, open a business checking account,) Tj
T* (then add 3 to 5 net-30 vendors. None of this touches personal credit and it supports every later application.) Tj
ET
